<title>LUXEMBOURG: Trial of ex-KB Luxembourg workers starts.</title>
<headline>Trial of ex-KB Luxembourg workers starts.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two former employees of Kredietbank (KB) Luxembourg, a unit of Belgium's Almanij holding company, went on trial on Monday on charges of illegally transferring funds to accounts in eastern Europe.</p>
<p>Of the 20 million marks ($13.1 million) involved, KB Luxembourg says it has recovered around 18.3 million marks.</p>
<p>The two were among five employees sacked by the bank at the start of 1994 after the fraudulent actions were detected.</p>
<p>The three others are not being prosecuted under Luxembourg law because they are residents of neighbouring Belgium.</p>
<p>The trial is expected to last all week.</p>
